ney dialysis and kidney transplant are two treatments for","options":["Misbalance in glomerular filtrate","kidney failure","kidney stones","Misbalance of osmoregulation"],"correctIndex":1,"page":39,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b1-elq-55803e02dc80df0e","chapterId":"el-b1-c11","topicId":"el-b1-t7-0","type":"mcq","text":"Kind of kidney dialysis in which fluid of dialysis is pumped into peritoneal cavity is _____","options":["Hypotonic dialysis","Vertebral dialysis","Peritoneal dialysis","Abdominal dialysis"],"correctIndex":2,"page":39,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b1-elq-2ff8a32b1f045acc","chapterId":"el-b1-c12","topicId":"el-b1-t8-0","type":"mcq","text":"Chemical coordination brought about by ________________.","options":["Stimuli","Endocrine system","Nervous system","Receptors"],"correctIndex":1,"page":47,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b1-elq-2cc74f160845f7be","chapterId":"el-b1-c12","topicId":"el-b1-t9-0","type":"mcq","text":"________ conduct impulses away from cell body","options":["Axons","Dendrites","Cell body","Schwann cells"],"correctIndex":0,"page":49,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b1-elq-f79869f7689e2fa2","chapterId":"el-b1-c12","topicId":"el-b1-t9-0","type":"mcq","text":"Between the areas of myelin on an axon, there are non-myelinated points, called the _______________.","options":["Schwann cells","myelin sheath","Nodes of Ranvier","Saltatory"],"correctIndex":2,"page":49,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b1-elq-bab135749fb66732","chapterId":"el-b1-c12","topicId":"el-b1-t9-0","type":"mcq","text":"_______ is present on top of medulla.","options":["Cerebellum","Medulla oblongata","Hypothalamus","Pons"],"correctIndex":3,"page":49,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b1-elq-cc9e3375beb6a234","chapterId":"el-b1-c12","topicId":"el-b1-t9-0","type":"mcq","text":"Spinal cord is the continuation of ____________.","options":["Medulla oblongata","Cerebellum","Hypothalamus","Thalamus"],"correctIndex":